  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.",
      "secondary_message": "1 mango\n1 (2 inch) piece ginger root\n1 lime\n½ small bunch green onion (scallion)\n½ small bunch cilantro\n½ small head red cabbage"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel mango and slice flesh away from the pit, starting with the flat sides; small dice the flesh. Divide between two medium bowls, then set one bowl aside for the slaw.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Using a fork or potato masher, mash mango in the remaining bowl until semi-smooth. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel and mince ginger and garlic. Add both to the bowl with the mashed mango. ",
      "secondary_message": "3 clove garlic"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add soy sauce, gochujang, sugar, vinegar, salt, and pepper to the bowl, then stir to combine the marinade.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "3 tbsp soy sauce\n3 tbsp gochujang\n7 tsp brown sugar\n1 tbsp rice wine vinegar\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Pat steak dry with paper towels, then slice crosswise into thin strips. Add to the bowl with the marinade, stir to coat, and set aside for 15 minutes.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, juice lime into the remaining bowl with the mango. Add sour cream, mayo, additional gochujang, sugar, salt, and pepper. Stir to combine the dressing.",
      "secondary_message": "¼ cup sour cream\n2 tbsp mayonnaise\ngochujang\n¼ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Using a clean cutting board, trim and cut green onions crosswise into thin pieces. Add to the bowl with the dressing.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Shave cilantro leaves off the stems; discard stems and roughly chop the leaves. Add to the bowl. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Halve cabbage lengthwise, cut out the core, and slice crosswise into thin (shred-like) strips. Add to the bowl, stir to combine the slaw, and set aside.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the steak is done marinating, preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Working in batches, add steak (leaving any excess marinade in the bowl) and stir-fry until cooked through, 4-5 minutes. Transfer steak to a plate.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tbsp toasted sesame oil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, warm tortillas in another skillet, oven, or microwave (optional).",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide tortillas between plates, then fill with slaw and beef. Sprinkle with sesame seeds and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": "4 tsp sesame seeds"
    }
  ],
